{
  "name": "discover-layer-hardware-absent",
  "description": "The same layer-narrowed `discover` over a project whose `hardware/` directory is not there: `present: false` — and no `optional` key, which in this default `summary` form means `false` — with the complete inventory published anyway. `present` is a probe's answer and not a declared default, so its `false` stays on the wire. The pair is the distinction an empty element list cannot express — no hardware declared at all, as against a layer whose elements happen to be zero — and since contract `2.0.0` the absent half is a project DEFECT: `check-model` reports it as `hardware.layer-absent`.",
  "kind": "example",
  "context": {
    "summary": "A project migrated from an earlier release, whose model has every other layer and no `hardware/` directory. It does not pass `check-model`; that is the state this exchange describes.",
